+    def _warmup_policy(self) -> None:
+        """Run one throwaway inference on zero-filled inputs.
+
+        torch.compile is lazy: with compile_model=True the graph is only built on the first real call,
+        which would otherwise happen with the robot already streaming -- the arm sits there while
+        Inductor autotunes. Doing it here moves that cost into server startup, where the client is
+        still blocked on SendPolicyInstructions and nothing is moving.
+
+        The dummy inputs mirror exactly what raw_observation_to_observation() produces at runtime --
+        same keys, same shapes, same dtype -- otherwise the compiled graph would be keyed on shapes
+        the real observations never hit and would simply be recompiled. In particular only the
+        cameras the client actually has are passed: padding features like empty_camera_N are
+        synthesised inside the policy, so adding them here would change the graph.
